summary:
  A look that comes hours late counts the whole gap as time the position stood.

history:
  The timer stands still while the machine sleeps, so the first look after
  a wake finds the position where it was and hours gone. A connection that
  survived a short sleep would be cut at that look; the standing starts
  anew instead, and a stream that is dead is found twenty seconds on.

target:
  package/contents/ui/StandLogic.js

find:
  late = nowMs - m.tickAt > 2 * TICK_MS || nowMs < m.tickAt;

replace:
  late = false;

expect:
  Killed by tst_standlogic::test_a_look_that_comes_late_starts_the_standing_anew.
  Line-neutral.
